      <title>Looking back: Queen Anne style house, early 1900s</title>
      <link>https://www.natchezdemocrat.com/opinion/looking-back-queen-anne-style-house-early-1900s-0c58f905</link>
      <description>This Queen Anne style house stands at 506 S. Union St. and was built in 1898 by Robert E. Bost for Charles and Bessie Patterson. Patterson was a partner in the retail business known as the Chamberlain and Patterson Staple and Fancy Dry Goods Store. It remained in the Patterson family until 1990.</description>
